<section id="summary">
<h2>Overview</h2>
<p>
    I am an Research Fellow at the <a href="https://aial.ie/">AI Accountability Lab (AIAL)</a> in <a href="https://www.tcd.ie/">Trinity College Dublin</a>. My research aims to understand the complexities that occur at the intersection of law (<i>data acquis</i> e.g. GDPR, AI Act), rights (privacy, data protection, consumer protection), and knowledge modelling (ontologies, taxonomies). My PhD (Computer Science, Trinity College Dublin) explored the application of linked data and semantic web technologies towards GDPR compliance, with a particular focus on consent and provenance.  I am a member of <a href="https://www.nsai.ie/">National Standards Authority of Ireland (NSAI)</a> and work on standardisation within the <a href="https://www.cencenelec.eu/">CEN/CENELEC</a> (EU) and <a href="https://www.iso.org/">ISO</a> subgroups on privacy and AI.</p>
    <p>I chair the <a href="https://www.w3.org/groups/cg/dpvcg/">W3C Data Privacy Vocabularies and Controls Community Group (DPVCG)</a> – which develops <a href="https://w3id.org/dpv">Data Privacy Vocabularies (DPV)</a> for legal and practical applications. I am the co-editor of the <a href="https://www.iso.org/standard/91775.html">ISO/IEC 27560 PII processing records standard</a>, am a nominated technical expert by the <a href="https://www.edpb.europa.eu/">European Data Protection Board (EDPB)</a>, and am a PI in the <a href="https://recitals-project.eu/">RECIALS Horizon project</a> and the <a href="https://harness-network.eu/">HARNESS Doctoral Network</a>.</p>
</p>
<p>See more about my:</p>
